<title>JAPAN: TOCOM to raise palladium futures margin fees.</title>
<headline>TOCOM to raise palladium futures margin fees.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo Commodity Exchange (TOCOM) said on Monday that it was raising margin requirements for all of its palladium futures contracts by 10,000 yen per trading lot, effective from Tuesday.</p>
<p>The move will bring the total March requirement to 84,250 yen, while margins for other months will rise to 59,500 yen, the TOCOM said in a statement. The increases are intended to cool overheated trade.</p>
<p>The TOCOM also said that it was restoring the daily price limit for palladium futures to 22 yen per gram from 33 yen, effective from Tuesday.</p>
</text>
